+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+This repo is the source of truth for the game. Studio is just where you run it. Rojo copies the
+files into your own dev place while you work. The [Layout table in the README](../README.md#layout)
+lists which folder becomes which instance.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools with Rokit: `rokit install` (versions are pinned in `rokit.toml`).
+2. Install packages with pesde: `pesde install`. This fills `roblox_packages/` and
+   `test_packages/roblox_packages/`. Both are git-ignored, so run it again after pulling changes to
+   `pesde.toml` or `test_packages/pesde.toml`.
+3. Install the Rojo plugin in Studio. Its version must match the `rojo` version in `rokit.toml`.
+4. Create your **own** dev place: open a new Baseplate in Studio and save it somewhere outside the
+   repo (or as your own private place). Don't share a place with a teammate. Two people syncing into
+   one place will overwrite each other's work.
+
+## Daily loop
+
+1. Pull, then run `pesde install` if the package manifests changed.
+2. Start the server from the project root: `rojo serve` (it uses `default.project.json` and port
+   34872 from `servePort`).
+3. In your dev place, open the Rojo plugin and click **Connect**.
+4. Edit files in `src/` in your editor. Rojo pushes each save into Studio within a moment.
+5. Playtest in Studio. When you're done, disconnect and stop `rojo serve`.
+
+## Where to make changes
+
+- **Code goes in files, never in Studio.** Anything Rojo manages (everything under the folders in
+  the Layout table) gets overwritten by the files on the next sync. If you edit a script in Studio,
+  your edit is lost and never reaches git.
+- Pick the folder by where the code runs:
+  - Server-only code: `src/ServerScriptService`
+  - Code shared by server and client: `src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared`
+  - Client code: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts`
+  - UI: `src/StarterGui`
+  - Jest specs: `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs`, named `Something.spec.luau`
+- The file suffix sets the script type: `.server.luau` makes a Script, `.client.luau` makes a
+  LocalScript, and plain `.luau` makes a ModuleScript.
+- **Never edit `roblox_packages/` or `test_packages/roblox_packages/`.** pesde regenerates them. To
+  add or bump a package, change `pesde.toml` (or `test_packages/pesde.toml` for test-only packages),
+  run `pesde install`, and require it through its link (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.X`, or
+  `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.X` for the Jest packages).
+- The baseplate and spawn are defined in `default.project.json`. Change them there, not in Studio.
+- Building or tweaking things in your dev place is fine for experiments. Before you rely on them,
+  move them into the repo (as files or project-file entries). Otherwise they exist only on your
+  machine.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **The `rojo serve` terminal.** Look for warnings and errors after each save, especially after
+  you add, rename or move files. If the project file is broken, `rojo serve` fails to start and
+  prints a parse error.
+- **The Rojo plugin.** It should say it's connected. If it shows a conflict or asks to overwrite
+  instances on connect, read the list first. Unexpected entries usually mean your place has drifted
+  or the project file maps something wrong.
+- **The Explorer tree.** It should match the README Layout table. In particular, check that:
+  - `ReplicatedStorage.Packages` holds the game packages (Vide, Charm, ...),
+  - `ServerScriptService.Tests` holds both `Specs` and `Packages` (Jest, JestGlobals),
+  - `ServerScriptService` has exactly **one** `Tests` folder,
+  - `StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts` holds `Main` and is not empty.
+- **The Output window.** Watch for require errors such as "is not a valid member", which usually
+  point at a mapping problem rather than a code problem.
+- Before you push, run the checks in the [README](../README.md#checks). `rojo sourcemap` is the
+  quickest way to see whether the project file is valid.
+
+## Keeping `default.project.json` healthy
+
+Most "it works on my machine" problems in this repo come from this one file. To keep it healthy:
+
+- **Only change it when the layout itself changes**, and update the README Layout table in the same
+  commit. The table and the file must always agree.
+- **Every `$path` must exist on disk.** A typo (for example `StarterPlayerScript` instead of
+  `StarterPlayerScripts`) maps an empty or missing folder, and nothing warns you in Studio.
+- **Keep `globIgnorePaths`.** `src/ServerScriptService` is mapped as a whole, and the project also
+  maps `ServerScriptService.Tests` explicitly so it can add `Tests.Packages`. The ignore entry
+  keeps Rojo from creating `Tests` twice. If you remove one, remove the other too.
+- **Jest packages live at `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`.** Specs and `jest.config` look for
+  them there. Don't move them to `ReplicatedStorage`.
+- **Save it as plain UTF-8 without a BOM, with LF line endings.** Rojo can't parse a file that
+  starts with a byte-order mark (it fails with "Failed to parse JSONC"). Some Windows editors and
+  merge tools add one silently. In VS Code, check the encoding in the status bar: it should say
+  `UTF-8`, not `UTF-8 with BOM`.
+- **Resolving merge conflicts:** don't just "accept both" or "accept theirs". Rebuild the file so it
+  matches the README table. Then run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts` and, if possible,
+  `rojo serve` and check the Explorer tree as described above before committing the resolution.
+- Ask for a review of any PR that touches `default.project.json`, and mention the change in the PR
+  description.
